# Simulated card checkout (full flow via API gateway :8080)

# REMEMBER TO PASTE THE JWT FROM THE LOGIN RESPONSE INTO THE @token VARIABLE <---------------------------------->

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@token = PASTE_JWT_HERE_FROM_AFTER_LOGIN
@orderId = PASTE_ORDER_ID_HERE_FROM_CREATE_ORDER_RESPONSE
@orderTotal = 51.00

### Register (optional if you already have a user)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "checkout-demo@example.com",
  "password": "password12"
}

### Login — copy accessToken into @token above
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "checkout-demo@example.com",
  "password": "password12"
}

### Who am I (optional)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Create order — requires JWT; userId in body is ignored (comes from token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/order
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "id": null,
  "userId": null,
  "orderNumber": null,
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": 102,
      "productName": "Demo items",
      "price": 25.50,
      "quantity": 2
    }
  ]
}

### Get order — expect status PENDING until checkout-card succeeds (set @orderId from create response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/order/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Card checkout — amount MUST match order totalPrice (e.g. 51.00 for two items at 25.50)
# Valid Luhn test card number: 4242424242424242
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/checkout-card
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "orderId": {{orderId}},
  "amount": {{orderTotal}},
  "cardNumber": "4242424242424242",
  "cardHolderName": "Demo User",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "cvv": "123"
}
